{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Everybody abstained{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1>When everybody abstains</h1>
    <p>
        No voter in this application claims <code>{{ unclaimed }}</code>, so every one of them
        abstains. A manager never hands an abstention back — it settles it — and what it settles on
        is the one thing that differs between these two rows.
    </p>
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th><code>allowIfAllAbstain</code></th><th>Verdict</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>true</code></td>
                <td>{{ lenient.isGranted ? '✅' : '⛔' }} <code>{{ lenient.decision.value }}</code></td>
                <td class="muted">{{ lenient.reason ?: '—' }}</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>false</code></td>
                <td>{{ strict.isGranted ? '✅' : '⛔' }} <code>{{ strict.decision.value }}</code></td>
                <td class="muted">{{ strict.reason ?: '—' }}</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">
        The policy that let this page render named <code>true</code> for its own request. The
        application-wide default belongs to the manager, and is declared under
        <code>security.access_decision_manager.allow_if_all_abstain</code> where there is a
        Security, or <code>access_control.allow_if_all_abstain</code> where there is not — naming it
        on both raises rather than one winning.
    </p>
{% endblock %}
